* What is Cloud Computing?
	The practice of using a network of remote servers hosed on the Internet to store, manage, and process
	data, rather than a local server or personal computer
		On-Premise
			You own the servers, hire the IT people, pay the rent, take all the risk
		Cloud Providers
			Someone else owns the servers, IT people, and rent, but you are responsible for
			configuring cloud services and code, someone else takes care of the rest

* The Evolution of Cloud Hosting
	Dedicated Server - One physical machine dedicated to a single business
		Very Expensive, High maintenance, High security
	Virtual Private Server (VPS) - The physical machine is virtualized into sub-machine
		Better utilization and isolation of resources
	Shared Hosting - One physical machine shared by hundreds of businesses
		Very cheap, limited functionality, poor isolation
	Cloud Hosting - Multiple physical machines that act as one system
		Flexibly, Scalable, secure, cost-effective, high configurability

* Common Cloud Services
	Four most common types of cloud services for IaaS
		Compute - Imagine having a virtual computer that can run application, programs and code
		Storage - Imagine having a virtual hard-drive that can store files
		Networking - Imagine having the virtual network being able to define internet connections or
				network isolations.
		Databases - Imagine a virtual database for storing reporting data or a database for general
				purpose web-application.

